71527 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186270415 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271527 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186271142 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271527 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186271193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271527 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271527 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271527 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186271142 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271527 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0c9c0040-57fa-5c39-be56-9379977d3577" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272031 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272031 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140133" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272031 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272031 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the eigenvectors of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $C$ given that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]C=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272031 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "74386825-044a-58dc-81f5-45db80c2e6c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272031 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]$ appears on both sides of the equation. Since this matrix is invertible (its determinant is not zero), left-multiplying the equation by the inverse gives the following expression for $C:$ \n\n$$\nC={{{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{P}{{[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{D}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $C$ is diagonalizable. The eigenvalues of $C$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=6$ and the corresponding eigenvectors are the columns of the matrix $P.$ Computing $P,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the corresponding eigenvectors are: \n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321727 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-14 & 30 \\\\ -9 & 19\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321727 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321727 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "49bb4f87-a553-5cdb-b80b-b631b4806733" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321902 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 16\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321902 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321902 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6043b6d5-2b00-5716-9a69-b16e9d93b380" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321910 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}70 & 32 \\\\ 32 & -52\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321910 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321910 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "616a24c3-6314-553b-9c11-cdb0a248bd5c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322694 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}6 & -12 \\\\ -4 & 24\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322694 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322694 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c780910b-6e0f-551e-a53d-4157c9a767da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322930 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}70 & -13 \\\\ 17 & -29\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322930 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322930 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e3a925df-9e30-5607-86c3-a1cf71d0b68e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323639 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323639 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323639 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321910 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323639 #edb/ref 1075